--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Training data sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tox21 (nuclear-receptor and stress-response endpoints)
  U.S. Tox21 program (NIH/NCATS, EPA, FDA, NTP). Public domain.
  https://tripod.nih.gov/tox21/

PubChem BioAssay — CYP450 inhibition
  Veith, H. et al. "Comprehensive characterization of cytochrome P450 isozyme
  selectivity across chemical libraries." Nat. Biotechnol. 27, 1050-1055 (2009).
  U.S. Government work; public domain.

FDA DICTrank — cardiotoxicity
  Liu, Z. et al. "DICTrank: FDA-curated drug-induced cardiotoxicity rank."
  Drug Discov. Today (2023). FDA public resource.

DILIrank — drug-induced liver injury
  Xu, J.J. et al. / FDA DILIrank dataset (2015). Public.

ChEMBL / AstraZeneca ADME datasets — plasma protein binding (ppbr_az),
hepatocyte and microsome clearance (clearance_hepatocyte_az,
clearance_microsome_az), lipophilicity (lipophilicity_astrazeneca)
  Released by AstraZeneca via ChEMBL. Source data licensed CC-BY-SA 3.0.
  ChEMBL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/  (EMBL-EBI)

AqSolDB — aqueous solubility (solubility_aqsoldb)
  Sorkun, M.C., Khetan, A., Er, S. "AqSolDB, a curated reference set of aqueous
  solubility." Sci. Data 6, 143 (2019). Source data licensed CC-BY 4.0.

Academic measurement datasets (via Therapeutics Data Commons)
  Caco-2 permeability — Wang, N.-N. et al. (2016)
  Human intestinal absorption — Hou, T. et al. (2007)
  Oral bioavailability — Ma, C.-Y. et al. (2008)
  Blood-brain barrier — Martins, I.F. et al. (2012)
  Volume of distribution — Lombardo, F., Jing, Y. (2016)
  Half-life — Obach, R.S. et al. (2008)
  Acute toxicity LD50 — Zhu, H. et al. (2009)
  CYP substrate — Carbon-Mangels, M., Hutter, M.C. (2011)
  P-glycoprotein substrate — Broccatelli, F. et al. / Wang, Z. et al.

Therapeutics Data Commons (benchmark splits)
  Huang, K. et al. "Therapeutics Data Commons: Machine Learning Datasets and
  Tasks for Drug Discovery and Development." NeurIPS (2021).
  https://tdcommons.ai/
